description: Require cleanup for Playwright tests that create E2E data
globs: tests/**/*.ts
alwaysApply: false
---

# E2E Data Teardown

- Any test that creates data (sessions, KB, tools, intakes, assistants, etc.) **must** clean it up.
- Prefer `trackCleanup` from `tests/helpers/smoke-test.ts` (fixture runs after the test, LIFO, including on failure).
- Keep delete/deactivate logic on page objects; `tests/helpers/smoke-cleanup.ts` is for shared UI delete helpers only.
- Use `smokeLabel()` (or equivalent unique names) so cleanup targets only test-owned data.
- Load/shell-only smokes do not need cleanup.
- If the product has no delete/archive path, document the gap in the spec and use the supported teardown (e.g. deactivate) or skip create until cleanup exists.
- New create-flow PRs must include cleanup in the same change set.

## Pattern

```ts
import { test, expect } from '../helpers/smoke-test';
import { smokeLabel } from '../helpers/smoke-data';

test('creates X and cleans up', async ({ page, trackCleanup }) => {
  const name = smokeLabel('x');
  const po = new SomePage(page);
  trackCleanup(async () => {
    await po.deleteX(name);
  });

  await po.goto();
  await po.createX({ name });
});
```

Register cleanups in creation order when multiple entities exist (LIFO tears down dependents first).
